 {"id": "S3-DEADLINE-001", "title": "[P1] Per-namespace S3 sync deadline is a fixed 300s — namespaces above ~560 objects can never be pushed or pulled", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:09:27Z", "reasoning": "BACKUP-RESTORE-PROOF-001 measured the engine at 0.53 s/object sequential against Hetzner hel1. The per-namespace deadline (src/s3/sync.ts namespaceDeadlineSeconds, default 300s, S3-GIT-007) therefore caps any single namespace at ~560 objects: chat-archive (617 objects) aborted at 570. Live namespaces above that cap: scheduler 258,672 syncable objects, pokemon-global 49,631, fleet-quality 29,091, coding-hermes 20,072, hermes-telemetry 14,810, relationships 10,016. Under shipped defaults those namespaces cannot be backed up or restored at all, so the DR runbook's RTO is 'never completes' rather than a slow number.", "acceptance_criteria": "(1) REPRODUCE with S3_SYNC_NAMESPACE_DEADLINE_S unset: duckbrain s3 sync chat-archive push to a throwaway prefix aborts with 'sync deadline exceeded after 300s' after 570 of 617 objects; transcript already in docs/evidence/backup-restore-proof-2026-11-05.md. (2) FIX so the shipped default covers the fleet's real namespaces: either derive the deadline from the work (object count x measured per-object cost, with a floor) or make transfers concurrent; the S3-GIT-007 protection must still abort a GENUINELY stuck namespace — prove with a black-holed endpoint or an injected stall that the run exits nonzero and names the namespace. (3) PROVE on a scratch prefix that scripts/restore-proof.sh --namespaces chat-archive PASSES end-to-end with NO deadline env override, and record the measured RTO for the 617-object namespace. (4) test-counts.json bumped in the same commit if the suite counts move.", "updated_at": "2026-11-06T01:29:33Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "9ede1a1d05b87d2c62e6226f7bf0dd721416191fb2bdbd18c82859a1e76169aa", "evidence": [{"run_id":"c5bc92a3","ts":"2026-11-06T01:29:33Z"}]}, "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "aa8b7b34", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": "claimed by harden-loop 2026-11-06T01:08:58Z; worktree wt/S3-DEADLINE-001\n\naa8b7b34 (on origin/main; ancestor verified + src/s3/sync-deadline-budget-s3deadline001.test.ts present in origin/main tree). Evidence run c5bc92a3 (gitreins judge: tier1 PASS, tier2 PASS, overall PASS). Mechanism: S3_SYNC_NAMESPACE_DEADLINE_S is no longer a total wall-clock cap — it is the NO-PROGRESS window, re-armed on every completed object (NamespaceDeadline), and the FLOOR of a work-derived total allowance (syncDeadlineBudgetSeconds = window + objects x 0.53s measured x 3 headroom); transfers run in a bounded pool (syncConcurrency, S3_SYNC_CONCURRENCY default 8, clamp 1..32); the abort names the namespace and the progress reached. PROVEN: (1) reproduced — evidence doc 'Defect 1' transcript with the var unset aborts '[S3] sync chat-archive timed out after 300s (S3-GIT-007)' at 570/617, and a re-run control on PRE-FIX origin/main src/s3/sync.ts (40 objects x 60ms, 1s window) fails 'sync deadline exceeded after 1s' while the fixed engine uploads all 40; (2) stuck still aborts: black-holed endpoint http://10.255.255.1:9000, 5s window => '[S3] sync probe timed out after 5s (S3-GIT-007)' + 'sync deadline exceeded after 5s for namespace probe (no progress for 5s...)' EXIT=1; (3) scripts/restore-proof.sh no longer exports an 1800s override, and with BOTH knobs unset '--namespaces chat-archive' PASSED: 617/617 objects, per-file sha256 identical for ALL 617, known-key read HTTP 200, MEASURED RTO 50.7s pull / 37.4s push (pre-fix: 277.4/329.8s and an abort at 570); (4) test-counts.json 259/2166 -> 260/2174 in the same commit, full suite 260 files / 2174 tests green, tsc --noEmit clean. NOT PROVEN: the large namespaces (scheduler 258,674 objects, ~5.9h at the measured rate) were not transferred end to end — the deadline now permits them, the wall clock